---
title: "Typography"
description: "Font, text layout, and text color."
section: Utilities
sectionOrder: 3
order: 5
---

Reach for a role first (`data-ui="text-lg"`, native headings), then override one property with a utility. `--font-weight` takes a number or the role weights `strong`, `heading`, and `body`; standard names such as `medium` are not CSS, so write `500`. Text color is `--text`, with state tiers.

`--text-wrap: truncate` keeps text on one line and ends the overflow with an ellipsis. It needs a width to overflow: a block element, a sized one (`--w: 48`), or a flex item with `--min-w: 0`, since a flex item can't shrink below its content otherwise. `none` means plain wrapping, so `--text-wrap: truncate; --text-wrap--md: none` wraps from `md` up. It takes breakpoints and states. It beats a primitive's own overflow while active, a tier with any other value hands that back, and `--overflow` wins over it. The exception is `--stuck`: another value there changes the wrapping but keeps the clip. A multi-word value like `wrap balance` isn't supported. To clamp to more than one line, use `--line-clamp`.

```html
<p style="--text-wrap: truncate">A file name far too long for its column.pdf</p>
```

